<title>THAILAND: Worker protest halts Karat operations.</title>
<headline>Worker protest halts Karat operations.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's sanitaryware producer Karat Sanitaryware Plc said on Friday a group of its employees had staged a protest at its plant in Saraburi, stopping normal operations.</p>
<p>The protesters at the plant, about 100 km (60 miles) north of Bangkok, demanded higher wages and better welfare, Karat said in a filing to the Stock Exchange of Thailand.</p>
<p>The bourse briefly halted trading in shares of Karat in the afternoon session, but said trading could resume after the announcement was made.</p>
